{"name":"Burlwood","hex":"#a17874","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"burlwood","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["burl (a type of wood on a tree)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burlwood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Burl","blocks":[{"text":"A burl or burr is a tree growth in which the grain has grown in a deformed manner. It is commonly found in the form of a rounded outgrowth on a tree trunk or branch that is filled with small knots from dormant buds. Burl formation is typically a result of some form of stress such as an injury or a viral or fungal infection. More scientifically, a burl is \"the result of hyperplasia, a greatly abnormal proliferation of xylem production by the vascular cambium\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Growth_on_tree_trunk_-_geograph.org.uk_-_724687.jpg/330px-Growth_on_tree_trunk_-_geograph.org.uk_-_724687.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burl","wikidata":"Q1483529"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Fatburl.jpeg/500px-Fatburl.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Fatburl.jpeg/1280px-Fatburl.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Fatburl.jpeg/500px-Fatburl.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Large burl on a spruce tree at Denali State Park, Alaska","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFatburl.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Burlrailingseats.JPG/500px-Burlrailingseats.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Burlrailingseats.JPG/1280px-Burlrailingseat